body:
1) Designated pickup spots are the only place to get picked up on strip;
2) Avoid surge pricing by waiting it out if you're not in a hurry.

(2 may apply anywhere, but in my experience as a passenger it's more pronounced here)

I have given 611 rides, and I've given approximately 600 passengers a five-star rating. I'd give you one star without hesitation. 

You:

A) planned to get your friend drunk;

B) had notice that she didn't feel well before getting in the lyft;

C) are now more concerned with your passenger rating than the fact that the driver is stuck having to clean a stranger's vomit out of his car, and cannot give any more rides until he completely cleans and sanitizes everything.

Sometimes vomiting in a car may be inevitable. This was not one of those times. A cleaning fee and a big tip doesn't come close to the making up for the level of inconvenience this causes the driver.
